{%- comment -%}
  Demo rating for one product, for presenting the design before any
  reviews exist. Outputs "rating|count", or nothing.

  Shared by the product card and the product page so a product shows the
  same numbers in both places. Derived from the product id, so it is
  stable from load to load.

  LOCKED to non-published themes: on the live (main) theme this renders
  nothing, whatever the setting says. A rating no customer gave is a
  fabricated review, and publishing one is an offence under the UK DMCC
  Act 2024. Callers check for a real reviews metafield first; this is only
  the fallback.

  Usage: {%- capture demo -%}{% render 'sp-demo-rating', id: product.id %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if theme.role != 'main' and id != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign demo_values = '4.5,4.6,4.4,4.8' | split: ','
    assign demo_i = id | modulo: 13 | modulo: 4
    assign demo_count = id | modulo: 87 | plus: 14
  -%}
  {{- demo_values[demo_i] }}|{{ demo_count -}}
{%- endif -%}
